skills/ (copied from the Rosetta kits, MIT)

Each folder holds a SKILL.md, a short DIGEST.md that the harness adds to the
first task message, and python3-stdlib helper scripts. All were written for
Rosetta; `kit_run` references were rewritten to plain `python3 skills/...`.

tdd, systematic-debugging, verification-before-completion, large-refactor
  The choice of methodologies follows the "superpowers" skill collection by
  Jesse Vincent (obra/superpowers, MIT License). No text or code was copied:
  the kits and their scripts were written for Rosetta. The kit format is
  compatible with Agent Skills (agentskills.io, Apache-2.0).

No kit copied here uses text adapted from K-Dense-AI/scientific-agent-skills
(MIT); those adaptations live only in the data-analysis, data-viz and
scientific-computing kits, which are not included.
